WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:15.473
Ben spent the next few days working harder than he'd ever worked before.

2
00:00:15.474 --> 00:00:23.894
On the day before the dress rehearsal, he was backstage with Winnie while she put finishing touches on the witches' black cauldron.

3
00:00:23.895 --> 00:00:31.950
"The cauldron looks amazing, Winnie," Ben said. "So do all the costumes."

4
00:00:31.951 --> 00:00:36.973
"Thanks. You were great during your last run-through," Winnie said.

5
00:00:36.974 --> 00:00:39.307
"Are you ready for the dress rehearsal?"

6
00:00:39.308 --> 00:00:41.437
"I think so," Ben replied.

7
00:00:41.438 --> 00:00:47.495
"I finally memorized my lines—without any help from Waldo." He laughed.

8
00:00:47.496 --> 00:00:51.561
"Uncle Bert told me to sleep with the script under my pillow.

9
00:00:51.562 --> 00:00:55.446
Apparently, that's what lots of Hollyweird actors do."

10
00:00:55.447 --> 00:00:58.412
"Whatever works," Winnie said.

11
00:00:58.413 --> 00:01:01.746
"Are you still worried about the curse?" Ben asked.

12
00:01:01.747 --> 00:01:07.539
She shrugged. "Not really. The show seems to be running smoothly now."

13
00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:11.888
Ben nodded. "Mog has finally stopped saying that name.

14
00:01:11.889 --> 00:01:16.042
And now that Jen has a headset, she doesn't have to move around so much.

15
00:01:16.043 --> 00:01:19.539
She's not leaving slime trails on the stage anymore."

16
00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:28.369
Winnie chuckled. "I'd better get the costumes onstage so everyone can see them before rehearsal starts."

17
00:01:28.370 --> 00:01:32.489
Winnie started to roll a large rack filled with costumes.

18
00:01:32.490 --> 00:01:35.343
"Want me to bring the cauldron?" Ben asked.

19
00:01:35.344 --> 00:01:41.018
"I'll get it later," Winnie said.

20
00:01:41.019 --> 00:01:46.225
A group of excited monsters immediately gathered around the costumes.

21
00:01:46.226 --> 00:01:53.148
"Ooh!" A purple monster pointed to a long white gown. "Look at that one!"

22
00:01:53.149 --> 00:01:56.754
"That's for Gaby," a skeleton said.

23
00:01:56.755 --> 00:02:03.169
Ozzy held up a soldier costume. "I can't wear this. It doesn't have arms!"

24
00:02:03.170 --> 00:02:09.500
"I'll take that, thank you." A long serpent monster snatched the costume with his fangs.

25
00:02:09.501 --> 00:02:14.446
He turned to Winnie. "This looks fabulous!"

26
00:02:14.447 --> 00:02:17.885
Winnie beamed. "I'm glad you like it, Miles."

27
00:02:17.886 --> 00:02:24.816
"Step aside!" Jade pushed through the crowd, along with the other two witches.

28
00:02:24.817 --> 00:02:28.875
"Where are our costumes?" Sonia asked.

29
00:02:28.876 --> 00:02:31.681
Winnie pulled three costumes off the rack.

30
00:02:31.682 --> 00:02:38.202
The long, dark gowns were covered with cobwebs and intricate beadwork spiders.

31
00:02:38.203 --> 00:02:43.790
Winnie drew in a nervous breath. "What do you think, witches?"

32
00:02:43.791 --> 00:02:49.213
Sonia was the first witch to speak. "We are going to look so good!"

33
00:02:49.214 --> 00:02:52.843
"I love the spiders!" Jade exclaimed.

34
00:02:52.844 --> 00:02:57.838
Ben grinned. "Your costumes are a hit, Winnie!" he whispered.

35
00:02:57.839 --> 00:03:01.049
"Can we try them on?" Lucy asked.

36
00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:04.780
"I think we should wait for Ms. Lafang," Winnie said.

37
00:03:04.781 --> 00:03:10.718
"Fine." Lucy tossed her hair. "What about our cauldron? Can we see that?"

38
00:03:10.719 --> 00:03:12.605
"Sure," Winnie said.

39
00:03:12.606 --> 00:03:14.830
"I'll go get it," Ben volunteered.

40
00:03:14.831 --> 00:03:19.244
Ben hurried backstage to retrieve the large papier-mâché cauldron.

41
00:03:19.245 --> 00:03:23.421
But as he bent to pick it up, a light flashed from onstage.

42
00:03:23.422 --> 00:03:26.238
"That was weird," he thought.

43
00:03:26.239 --> 00:03:30.621
As Ben headed back toward the others, the light flashed again.

44
00:03:30.622 --> 00:03:32.524
Then he saw what had caused it.

45
00:03:32.525 --> 00:03:43.563
While Winnie helped the octopus monster into her costume, the witches were admiring themselves in a handheld mirror.

46
00:03:43.564 --> 00:03:46.142
"No mirrors!" Ben cried.

47
00:03:46.143 --> 00:03:52.689
He zipped across the stage toward the mirror, without stopping to think—or see the two skeletons in his way.

48
00:03:52.690 --> 00:03:58.273
Boom! Ben crashed into the two skeletons, sending them clattering to the ground.

49
00:03:58.274 --> 00:04:06.368
He struggled to hold onto the big cauldron, but it slipped from his hands and rolled right into the rack of costumes.

50
00:04:06.369 --> 00:04:15.762
"Ahh!" Winnie shrieked as the rack went rolling into a stack of open paint cans at the other side of the stage.

51
00:04:15.763 --> 00:04:20.389
Everyone watched in disbelief as the paint cans flew through the air.

52
00:04:20.390 --> 00:04:24.859
"No!" A big blue monster got hit with green paint.

53
00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:27.441
A ghoul became pink.

54
00:04:27.442 --> 00:04:32.802
And the cauldron—along with every costume on the rack—was covered in . . .

55
00:04:32.803 --> 00:04:41.712
Ben gasped. "Bright blue paint! Remember the superstition—we can't have blue costumes!"

56
00:04:41.713 --> 00:04:45.620
"Our beautiful costumes!" Sonia cried.

57
00:04:45.621 --> 00:04:50.058
"Ben!" Lucy balled her fists and glowered at him.

58
00:04:50.059 --> 00:04:54.164
"You ruined everything . . . again!"

59
00:04:54.165 --> 00:04:59.679
"I'm sorry!" Ben cried. "But mirrors are bad luck onstage, and—"

60
00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:05.857
"Students!" Mr. Freaky shouted, racing into the auditorium.

61
00:05:05.858 --> 00:05:17.548
"What's going on?" Abruptly he halted, his noses wiggling as he stared in shock at the damage.

62
00:05:17.549 --> 00:05:20.203
"Who did this?"

63
00:05:20.204 --> 00:05:23.632
The witches and a few others spun toward Ben.

64
00:05:23.633 --> 00:05:26.406
"Ben did it!" Lucy snapped.

65
00:05:26.407 --> 00:05:32.781
"Mirrors and blue costumes might be bad luck onstage—but he's even worse!"

66
00:05:32.782 --> 00:05:37.247
Heat flooded Ben's face. "It's true, Mr. Freaky.

67
00:05:37.248 --> 00:05:39.129
I was worried about the mirror.

68
00:05:39.130 --> 00:05:42.326
I just wanted to get it offstage before something terrible . . ."

69
00:05:42.327 --> 00:05:52.304
Ben tried to keep defending himself, but then he saw the tears streaming down Winnie's face.

70
00:05:52.305 --> 00:05:54.508
He snapped his mouth closed.

71
00:05:54.509 --> 00:06:02.052
Her beautiful costumes and cauldron were ruined, and it was all his fault.

72
00:06:02.053 --> 00:06:12.876
While everyone shouted and yelled, Mr. Freaky buried his face in his hands and moaned.

73
00:06:12.877 --> 00:06:18.064
Ben floated backstage and slipped out through a back wall.

74
00:06:18.065 --> 00:06:21.547
"I don't know if the curse is real or not," he thought.

75
00:06:21.548 --> 00:06:24.152
"But I don't belong anywhere near a stage.

76
00:06:24.153 --> 00:06:36.129
I'm going to find a hole to crawl into—and never come out!"

